{
  "name": "Auto-Respond to PR Comments",
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "description": "Detects the current repo and branch from git, finds the associated open PR, and responds to all unanswered review comments automatically.",
  "when": {
    "type": "userTriggered"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Auto-detect the PR and respond to comments. Steps: 1) Run 'git remote get-url origin' to get the GitHub remote URL. Parse owner and repo from it (handle both https://github.com/owner/repo.git and git@github.com:owner/repo.git formats). 2) Run 'git branch --show-current' to get the current branch name. 3) Use list_pull_requests with the owner/repo to find the open PR where head branch matches the current branch. If no PR found for this branch, tell the user. 4) Use get_pull_request to get full PR context (title, body, changed files). 5) Use list_pr_review_comments to get all inline review comments. 6) Use list_pr_comments to get conversation comments. 7) Build a reply chain — identify which comments already have replies by checking inReplyToId. 8) For each UNANSWERED comment: a) Read the file at the path mentioned in the comment from the local workspace. b) Understand what the reviewer is asking. c) Post a reply using reply_to_pr_review_comment for inline comments or create_pr_comment for general comments. 9) Skip trivial comments (LGTM, thanks, looks good, thumbs up emoji). Never reply to bot comments or your own previous replies. Format replies as: brief acknowledgment + explanation/justification."
  }
}
